course: dictionary
lesson: 6253
title: Moisture, the water all around us
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Moisture means small amounts of water or other liquid. It can be in the air, in the ground, or on a surface. A puddle is a lot of water, but the damp you feel on a cold day is moisture.
explain: Context shows you where moisture is. «It can snow at very low temperatures; very cold air holds little moisture, so heavy snow is less likely.» The clue is holds little: moisture is the water that air can carry, so less of it means less snow.
explain: Scientists and machines measure moisture. «A plant robot waters when moisture is below 30» means the robot has a sensor that reads the moisture in the soil, and it waters the plant only when the number drops under 30.
fact: Moisture is small amounts of water or other liquid in the air, in the ground, or on a surface.
fact: Moisture in the air, called humidity, can form dew, mist and clouds.
fact: Plants take moisture from the soil, and mould grows where there is moisture.
fact: Moisture on the inside of a cold window is called condensation.
fact: Searing meat browns it and adds flavour, but it does not seal in the moisture.
exercise: «Very cold air holds little moisture, so heavy snow is less likely.» What is moisture? | A cloud that is high in the sky | A kind of heavy snow | A type of very cold weather | *Small amounts of water or other liquid
exercise: A plant robot waters when moisture is below 30. Its readings are 40, 28 and 35. Which reading makes it water? | 50 | 40 | 35 | *28
exercise: Moisture on the inside of a cold window has a special name. What is it? | Sunshine | Thunder | *Condensation | Sand
test: A machine has no eyes or skin, only sensors. A moisture sensor turns moisture into what? | *A number the code can test | A smell | Music | A colour
test: Searing meat seals in the juices. Is this true? | Yes, it makes the meat wetter | No, searing makes meat cold | Yes, the juices stay in the meat | *No, seared meat loses as much moisture as unseared meat
exam: Which word means small amounts of water or other liquid in the air, in the ground or on a surface? | Mould | *Moisture | Humidity sensor | Condensation
